## 6. Boundaries

### [CXC-BIND-BOUNDARY] What Is NOT In the Config

- decision: **No arbitrary inline code** (e.g. inline Python) in `.compose.yaml`.
- rationale: it breaks define-once (Python can't run on the CYD/C++ or a TS-browser backend) and is an RCE surface on a fetch-from-bus display fleet. ESPHome's inline-C++ works only because it compiles to ONE runtime; ComposeUX is define-once-render-many.
- escape-hatch: real computation lives in a **bus workload** — a process that computes and publishes a namespace, which a widget then binds. Compute where it belongs; the config stays declarative and portable.
- deferred: a **sandboxed, restricted expression DSL** (HA-Jinja-flavored: arithmetic, `ns()` lookups, conditionals; interpretable identically on Python AND CYD/JS) is the sanctioned middle ground for the last ~10%, but it is a separate, **use-case-gated** deliverable ([CXC-RM-BEHAVIORS]) — collect ~5 real high-need cases first. This spec is the declarative 90%.
- test (negative): a config carrying an inline-code field is rejected or ignored, never executed.
- implemented: `bindings.strip_code_fields` removes code-shaped keys (code/script/python/eval/exec/expr/template/lambda/js/…) from every widget spec and behavior entry at parse time, with a logged [CXC-BIND-BOUNDARY] warning; `bindings.validate_map` refuses maps that are non-dicts or carry template/expression-shaped strings (`{{…}}`, `${…}`, leading `=`) — the whole binding is dropped, the attribute keeps its literal. Verified with an import-side-effect canary: the payload file is never created (test_c7).
- status: operational (2026-07-06).
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-BIND]

---

## 7. Composer Exposure

### [CXC-BIND-COMPOSER] The Binding Editor Authors This Model

- role: The Composer binding editor (next Composer slug, DP-CXC-3) exposes this model visually — pick a namespace, pick a behavior, set params — never typing raw YAML. This spec defines the model that UI configures; building the model first lets the editor expose bindings + transforms + behaviors in one pass.
- status: operational (2026-07-07) — [SPEC:CXC-BINDEDIT] built: the WC Bindings tab authors every form in this spec (bare-string/object bindings, literal maps, all trigger kinds incl. is_exact, the full behavior library with schema-driven params) and the WW previews them live on the design bus; C1–C8 PASS, Intelligence-over-MQTT 8/8. NOTE (ops): the Composer's MQTT client_id is now unique per process (`composeux-m4-<pid>`) — two Composers sharing an id kicked each other off the broker (rc=7 ping-pong), silently dropping command events while retained states survived.
- see-also: [CXC-BIND-ATTR], [CXC-BIND-BEHAVIOR], [SPEC:CXC-BINDEDIT]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-BIND]

